Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.20,0:00:02.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,Sweden built a warship so powerful…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.70,0:00:04.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,…it sank on its first voyage.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.20,0:00:06.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,The king wanted two gun decks. Sixty-four cannons.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.00,0:00:09.30,Cap,,0,0,0,,First, a test: thirty men ran across the deck.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.90,0:00:16.10,Cap,,0,0,0,,She rolled so hard, the admiral stopped the test.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.40,0:00:18.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,They sailed anyway.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.10,0:00:23.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,A breeze. She leaned… and came back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.20,0:00:25.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then, a stronger gust.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.00,0:00:27.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,The lower gunports were open.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:31.00,0:00:33.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,Within sight of the city, she sank.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.60,0:00:35.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,At least thirty people died.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:35.60,0:00:37.00,Cap,,0,0,0,,The designer was dead.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:37.20,0:00:39.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,The builders said the king approved the plans.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:39.60,0:00:40.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Nobody was punished.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.00,0:00:42.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,She sank in twenty minutes.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.80,0:00:45.60,Cap,,0,0,0,,Then she lay underwater for 333 years…
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.00,0:00:47.80,Cap,,0,0,0,,…until they brought her back,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:48.20,0:00:49.40,Cap,,0,0,0,,almost whole.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.20,0:00:06.80,Note,,0,0,0,,STOCKHOLM · 1628
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.80,0:00:20.90,Note,,0,0,0,,10 AUGUST 1628
